    <!-- ━━━━━━━━━━━━ Connection help dialog ━━━━━━━━━━━━ -->
    <string name="help_para_puck_slots">The controller uses the right Puck slot by default, and pairing it to another receiver replaces whatever is stored in that slot. To keep two Puck pairings at once, switch into left-slot wireless mode before you pair the second one. After that you can move between the two freely.</string>
    <string name="help_para_bt_independent">A Bluetooth pairing is stored separately from the Puck slots, so it survives re-pairing either of them.</string>
    <string name="help_para_power_off">The controller wakes into the connection it used last. To turn it off, hold the Steam button for about 5 seconds, until the chime sounds and the LED goes out.</string>
    <string name="help_section_wireless">Switching wireless modes</string>
    <string name="help_para_wireless_intro">Start with the controller off, then power it on holding one of these:</string>
